format: loopthing/container-v0.3
title: The Missing Artifact
kind: portable-thinking-container
created: 2026-04-29T07:18:00Z
entry: User Prompts/Master Prompt.md
origin: OpenAI Codex hackathon demo
mimetype: application/vnd.loopthing+zip

summary:
  A .loopthing is a single portable container for AI work: a forkable,
  auditable record of the user prompts, decisions, killed branches,
  journey map, and artifacts behind how an idea arrived.

lineage:
  - Began as a static OpenAI Codex hackathon viewer.
  - Used OpenClaw as the first source artifact.
  - Tried a GitHub repo input direction.
  - Killed "LoopThing a repo" because the repo is not the thinking process.
  - Landed on a portable container whose spine is user prompts plus artifacts.

principles:
  - One .loopthing file is the shareable container
  - loopthing-source/ is only the unpacked editing source
  - User Prompts is the canonical spine
  - Not a raw chat dump
  - Not a repo diff
  - Killed branches make the sharer look clearer, not messier
  - Produced artifacts travel with the thought process

files:
  - User Prompts/Master Prompt.md
  - User Prompts/Raw User Prompts.md
  - User Prompts/Prompt Change Log.md
  - Thought Process/Sanitized Thought Process.md
